  "findings": [
    "Largest energy deviation: Fe22+ 2s2p 3P is -17.3% vs NIST (43.804 vs 52.961 eV).",
    "Degenerate multiplets are truncated: the 4-state manifolds keep only 2/3 2s2p 3P components for Be, 1/3 2s2p 1P components for Be, 2/3 2s2p 3P components for C2+, 1/3 2s2p 1P components for C2+, 2/3 2s2p 3P components for Fe22+, 1/3 2s2p 1P components for Fe22+. Channel cross sections are undercounted by the missing components; raise n_states to capture the full terms.",
    "Fe XXIII has a 15.3 eV 3P fine-structure spread that the non-relativistic CASCI cannot reproduce (it returns a single degenerate level).",
    "Transition dipoles are systematically low by a near-constant factor (|mu|_computed/|mu|_reference = 0.61, 0.59), so absolute cross sections are underestimated by roughly that factor squared while the Z-scaling exponent is largely preserved.",
